{"name":"Barbarian","hex":"#f78c5a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barbarian","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to people, countries, or customs perceived as uncivilized or inferior."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A non-Greek or a non-Roman citizen.","An uncivilized or uncultured person, originally compared to the hellenistic Greco-Roman civilisation; usually associated with senseless violence and self-harm or other such shows of brute force and lack of mental faculty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbarian"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barbarian","blocks":[{"text":"A barbarian is, etymologically, a foreigner, specifically someone whose language and customs differ from those of the speaker. In ancient Greece, the term designated non-Greeks, while in the Roman world it referred more generally to peoples living outside the cultural and political sphere of the empire. In modern English, the word has developed a pejorative sense, commonly meaning a \"rude, wild, or uncivilized person\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Visigoths_sack_Rome.jpg/330px-Visigoths_sack_Rome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbarian","wikidata":"Q134313"},{"title":"Barbarian (2022 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Barbarian is a 2022 American horror film written and directed by Zach Cregger in his solo screenwriting and directorial debut. It is produced by Arnon Milchan, Roy Lee, Raphael Margules, and J. D. Lifshitz. The film stars Georgina Campbell, Bill Skarsgård, and Justin Long. The story follows a woman who rents a house on Airbnb and discovers a dark secret inside."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Barbarian_2022_film_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbarian_(2022_film)","wikidata":"Q38526439"}],"